# env: PATH=${MNML_SHIMS}/ai:${PATH}
# Right-click the cluster's Claude chip: the launcher rows, then `Icon`
# with the two branded choices under it and the current one ticked. The
# shipped icon is the Claude Code figure 󱸀 (U+F1E00); the alternate is
# the Anthropic spark 󱸂 (U+F1E02). Two choices, no glyph picker.
#
# Each row DRAWS the icon it picks, in the menu's glyph column: you
# pick by the picture, and the label only says whose it is. (They both
# used to draw a paint brush, which told you nothing.)
#
# Picking one changes the mark EVERYWHERE the chrome draws it in the
# same frame — the cluster chip here and a Claude pty tab below —
# because every painter reads `claude_mark.mark` rather than naming a
# codepoint.
#
# `tools/shims/ai/claude` stands in for the CLI (it sleeps), so the
# chip shows without the real binary. The mark sits at column 106 of
# the strip (`cluster_claude_chip.test`).
write a.txt "alpha alpha"
open a.txt
expect screen contains "󱸀"
expect screen lacks "󱸂"
rightclick 106 1
expect screen contains "Toggle existing Claude Code pane"
expect screen contains "Icon"
# `Icon` is the menu's last row, so End reaches it however many rows
# precede; Right opens the submenu.
key end
key right
expect screen contains "Claude Code"
expect screen contains "Anthropic"
expect screen contains "✓ Claude Code"
expect screen lacks "✓ Anthropic"
# The glyph column carries the mark each row would set — the figure on
# one row, the spark on the other, not one brush on both.
expect screen contains "󱸀  ✓ Claude Code"
expect screen contains "󱸂  Anthropic"
# Down then Enter — the second row, the spark.
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "Claude icon: Anthropic spark"
expect screen contains "󱸂"
expect screen lacks "󱸀"
# The tick moved with the key.
rightclick 106 1
key end
key right
expect screen contains "✓ Anthropic"
expect screen lacks "✓ Claude Code"
key esc
expect screen lacks "Toggle existing Claude Code pane"
# A Claude pty tab wears the chosen mark too, not the figure: one
# resolver, every surface. (`tools/shims/ai/claude` is the session.)
command view.toggle_tree
command ai.claude_code_new
wait 400
expect pane claude
expect screen contains "󱸂 claude 󰅖"
expect screen lacks "󱸀 claude 󰅖"
# And back: the figure returns everywhere in the same frame, tab and
# cluster chip together.
rightclick 106 1
key end
key right
key enter
expect screen contains "Claude icon: Claude Code figure"
expect screen contains "󱸀 claude 󰅖"
expect screen lacks "󱸂"
